⍝@ test3.

      ⎕UCS '⍴A B'
9076 65 32 66

      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ ⎕UCS with mixed arguments is a GNU APL extension
      ⎕UCS 'Hello',72 101 108 108 111
72 101 108 108 111 Hello

      ⍝ Regression (2026-08-10): ISO-IEC/JTC1/SC22 N3067 "APL Character
      ⍝ Repertoire" (devel_doc/n3067.pdf) lists 6 APL functional symbols
      ⍝ GNU APL previously had no UNI_xxx name for at all: ⊆ ⊇ ∅ ⍌ ⍓ ⍔.
      ⍝ None of them are assigned a function by any known APL dialect
      ⍝ (same category as e.g. ⍚/DIAMOND_UNDERBAR), so they are not ⎕AV
      ⍝ members and cannot be used as bare tokens in source -- but as
      ⍝ character DATA they must round-trip correctly, which is what
      ⍝ n3067 (in the context of ⎕TF/⎕IN/⎕OUT interchange) actually cares
      ⍝ about.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      V←⎕UCS 8838 8839 8709 9036 9043 9044
      V
⊆⊇∅⍌⍓⍔

      (⎕UCS V)≡8838 8839 8709 9036 9043 9044
